WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.577 --> 00:00:20.246
The next morning, when Ally got to work, Randy and Flo were standing behind the counter speaking in

2
00:00:20.306 --> 00:00:21.026
low voices.

3
00:00:21.046 --> 00:00:24.548
"Good morning," Ally said cheerfully.

4
00:00:24.568 --> 00:00:27.910
"Oh, hi," Randy said.

5
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.752
But Flo barely greeted Ally before they both went back to work.

6
00:00:35.756 --> 00:00:38.618
"That's odd," Ally thought, tying on her apron.

7
00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.359
"Are they mad at me?

8
00:00:40.919 --> 00:00:41.559
But why?

9
00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:46.762
Oh! Maybe Flo's upset that Ray went on vacation without her."

10
00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:50.024
But that didn't feel right either.

11
00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:52.746
Flo and Ray hadn't been dating that long.

12
00:00:53.526 --> 00:00:54.407
Then it hit her.

13
00:00:54.427 --> 00:00:59.990
"Flo is probably upset that Dawn is back," Ally thought.

14
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.612
Just then Jerry and Sally walked into the diner.

15
00:01:05.412 --> 00:01:07.973
"Barry asked us to meet him here," Jerry said.

16
00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:11.275
"While we wait, we'd like to shoot some footage of the diner."

17
00:01:11.295 --> 00:01:13.857
"No problem," Ally said.

18
00:01:13.877 --> 00:01:16.018
"Just don't film Flo."

19
00:01:16.978 --> 00:01:18.759
Soon Barry arrived, grinning.

20
00:01:18.779 --> 00:01:20.660
"I came up with a new dish.

21
00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.962
It's guaranteed to be something no one else will have."

22
00:01:23.982 --> 00:01:27.224
"You mean like Gorphelian Glug?"

23
00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:28.164
Ally asked.

24
00:01:30.105 --> 00:01:32.006
Everyone gave Ally a strange look.

25
00:01:32.026 --> 00:01:34.748
"Tee-hee!" Ally blushed.

26
00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:36.297
"Just kidding.

27
00:01:37.657 --> 00:01:38.798
What's your idea, Barry?"

28
00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:40.959
"Crater Cakes!"

29
00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:42.640
Barry said proudly.

30
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.781
"What are those?"

31
00:01:45.302 --> 00:01:45.922
Randy asked.

32
00:01:45.942 --> 00:01:49.284
"Peanut butter and marshmallow hand pies.

33
00:01:50.745 --> 00:01:53.546
I bet everyone else will be making main course dishes.

34
00:01:54.386 --> 00:01:57.288
While Rolling Ray's is the only one serving dessert!"

35
00:01:57.308 --> 00:02:00.870
"That's a cool idea," Ally said.

36
00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.192
"I'm going to the truck to make a test batch," Barry said.

37
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.140
"Mind if we come along?"

38
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.021
Jerry asked.

39
00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:08.501
"We'd like to film you."

40
00:02:08.521 --> 00:02:10.782
"Sure!" Barry said.

41
00:02:10.802 --> 00:02:12.002
"Let's go!"

42
00:02:18.424 --> 00:02:22.245
At work, Ally didn't get a chance to ask Flo if something was wrong.

43
00:02:22.825 --> 00:02:26.927
As she walked into her room later, she told herself that she would try again soon.

44
00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.688
For now, she had to get ready for tonight's double date.

45
00:02:31.712 --> 00:02:34.213
"Should I wear my hair in a ponytail or down?"

46
00:02:34.593 --> 00:02:35.553
Ally asked Alpha.

47
00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:40.014
"Hair is for humans, not Astralians," Alpha said.

48
00:02:40.034 --> 00:02:43.195
"I know, but I like having it."

49
00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:47.816
Ally started brushing her hair when a thought stopped her.

50
00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:53.958
"What if, once he gets to know me, Julius decides he doesn't like me?"

51
00:02:54.938 --> 00:02:55.618
Alpha lit up.

52
00:02:55.638 --> 00:02:58.359
"That is in the realm of possibility."

53
00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.980
"Alpha!" Ally said.

54
00:03:01.732 --> 00:03:03.673
"You're supposed to be nice to me."

55
00:03:03.693 --> 00:03:05.794
"Nice does not compute.

56
00:03:06.315 --> 00:03:08.196
Truth does," Alpha said.

57
00:03:08.216 --> 00:03:15.780
"Ugh!" Ally changed her clothes and tugged at her new outfit.

58
00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.002
"You're not really helping me with my nervousness."

59
00:03:19.022 --> 00:03:21.884
"Nervousness is an irrational response!"

60
00:03:22.344 --> 00:03:23.085
Alpha snapped.

61
00:03:23.885 --> 00:03:24.546
Ally frowned.

62
00:03:24.566 --> 00:03:25.626
"You know what?

63
00:03:26.106 --> 00:03:28.468
I think I'll leave you home tonight to charge up."

64
00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.981
Before Alpha could reply, Mateo knocked on the door.

65
00:03:32.001 --> 00:03:34.342
"Are you ready to head to the park, Ally?"

66
00:03:34.642 --> 00:03:35.062
he called.

67
00:03:35.082 --> 00:03:38.723
"Julius and Bethany are meeting us there with some picnic food."

68
00:03:38.743 --> 00:03:41.144
"Yes," Ally called back.

69
00:03:41.164 --> 00:03:44.325
"I'll be ready as soon as I power down Alpha.

70
00:03:44.985 --> 00:03:46.626
She's acting glitchy again!"

71
00:03:51.347 --> 00:03:53.628
On the way to the park, Mateo's phone pinged.

72
00:03:57.976 --> 00:04:03.099
He had a text from Barry: I spent three hours developing the recipe for the hand pies.

73
00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:04.800
They turned out fantastic!

74
00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.982
"That's great," Ally said.

75
00:04:08.002 --> 00:04:09.223
"It is!"

76
00:04:09.643 --> 00:04:11.344
Mateo said as he scrolled down.

77
00:04:11.364 --> 00:04:13.946
"Or maybe not.

78
00:04:14.726 --> 00:04:15.526
Look at this."

79
00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:21.250
But then Jerry told me that the Food Dude announced they're serving chocolate-filled hand pies!

80
00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:24.452
"Ugh," Ally groaned.

81
00:04:25.036 --> 00:04:30.098
"That's the second time another team came up with a dish that's just like ours."

82
00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:33.279
She halted and looked at Mateo.

83
00:04:33.299 --> 00:04:37.041
"Is it me, or does that seem really strange?

84
00:04:38.161 --> 00:04:40.622
It can't be just a coincidence, can it?"

85
00:04:40.642 --> 00:04:45.544
"I was thinking the same thing," Mateo said with a frown.

86
00:04:45.564 --> 00:04:48.405
"Something fishy is going on around here."

87
00:04:48.425 --> 00:04:50.606
"And chocolaty!"

88
00:04:50.987 --> 00:04:51.487
Ally said.

89
00:04:51.507 --> 00:04:55.504
"I think there's a mole," Mateo said.

90
00:04:55.524 --> 00:04:59.046
"What do moles have to do with this?"

91
00:04:59.506 --> 00:05:00.086
Ally asked.

92
00:05:00.106 --> 00:05:01.807
"Don't they live underground?"

93
00:05:01.827 --> 00:05:06.109
"Not that kind of a mole," Mateo said.

94
00:05:06.129 --> 00:05:09.450
"I mean a mole, like a spy.

95
00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.691
Maybe someone is feeding information to the other teams."

96
00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:14.332
Ally gasped.

97
00:05:15.012 --> 00:05:18.694
"I can't believe anyone would do that!"

98
00:05:18.714 --> 00:05:23.516
"Me neither, but it's the only explanation," Mateo said.

99
00:05:24.348 --> 00:05:24.969
Ally nodded.

100
00:05:24.989 --> 00:05:31.033
"We've got to figure out who it is, or we'll lose the contest before it even begins.

101
00:05:31.914 --> 00:05:33.475
But how do you catch a spy?

102
00:05:33.955 --> 00:05:35.877
We don't have them on Astralia."

103
00:05:35.897 --> 00:05:41.701
"I guess it's hard to keep secrets when everyone can read minds," Mateo said.

104
00:05:41.721 --> 00:05:43.382
"That's it!"

105
00:05:43.703 --> 00:05:44.303
Ally cried.

106
00:05:44.323 --> 00:05:48.846
"I'll read everyone's minds to find out who's spying on us!"

107
00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:56.216
"Everyone?" Mateo gestured to the people who were pouring into the park to watch the eclipse.

108
00:05:56.236 --> 00:06:02.021
"If that's what it takes," Ally said firmly, "that's what I'll do!

109
00:06:03.202 --> 00:06:04.984
And I'm going to start right now.

110
00:06:05.905 --> 00:06:09.048
Any one of these people here in Sandville could be the spy!"
